Some shared utilities in src/mcp_security_review/utils/ (env.py, io.py,
lifecycle.py, logging.py, tools.py) and the server scaffolding in
src/mcp_security_review/servers/ are adapted from mcp-atlassian
(https://github.com/sooperset/mcp-atlassian), licensed under the MIT License,
Copyright (c) 2024 Hyeonsoo Lee. The upstream license text is preserved in
LICENSE.

The threat library in src/mcp_security_review/library/ refers to requirement ids
from the OWASP Application Security Verification Standard (ASVS) 5.0.0
(https://github.com/OWASP/ASVS, CC BY-SA 4.0), to ids from the OWASP MCP Top 10 2025
(https://github.com/OWASP/www-project-mcp-top-10, CC BY-SA 4.0), and to MITRE CWE
identifiers (https://cwe.mitre.org). Only identifiers are used; all descriptive text
is original.

All other code, including everything under src/mcp_security_review/security/
and src/mcp_security_review/providers/sca/, is original to this project.

This project fetches MITRE ATT&CK technique, group, and software ids and data
at runtime from the ATT&CK STIX repository (https://github.com/mitre/cti),
subject to the ATT&CK Terms of Use (https://attack.mitre.org/resources/terms-of-use/),
and fetches mapping data at runtime from the Center for Threat-Informed
Defense (CTID) Mappings Explorer (https://github.com/center-for-threat-informed-defense/mappings-explorer),
licensed under the Apache License 2.0. Only identifiers are used; all
descriptive text is original.

This project imports the `cvss` package (https://pypi.org/project/cvss/)
unmodified, licensed under the GNU Lesser General Public License v3.0 or
later (LGPL-3.0+).
